& [AuthorizedFileSet] is exact
  + [production] is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/platform_preflight_forms.rs
  + [governance] is source, canonical, exploded, justification, plan, matrix, slice, registry, evidence, solution, proof, review, fault, file-change, turn, map, narrative, and reentry records
  - never: change lib.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, topology_forms.rs, or another production module

& [RequestContract] is strict and effect free
  + [type] is WindowsPlatformPreflightRequest
  + [request_profile] is exactly cantor-windows-platform-preflight-request/0.1
  + [result_profile] is exactly cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.2
  + [target_triple] is exactly x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
  + [input_root] reuses the existing canonical extended-DOS drive-root validator
  + [validation] uses ValidatePlatformPreflightForm and decode_platform_preflight_json
  + [effect] is zero

& [ResultContract] is one closed four-variant sum
  + [open_fault] contains common result identity and nonzero operating-system error code
  + [query_fault] adds one closed query stage and nonzero operating-system error code
  + [observation_fault] adds one closed query stage and one closed local fault class only
  + [complete] retains strong identity, canonical final path, volume, remote protocol, and disposition
  + [profile] is 0.2 for every variant
  + [partial_evidence] is absent from every fault

& [LocalFaultContract] is exact
  + [returned_length_limit] is admitted
  + [invalid_utf16] is admitted
  + [invalid_observation] is admitted
  + [other_class] rejects
  + [error_code] is not a field
  + [arbitrary_message] is not a field

& [OperatingSystemFaultContract] is provenance preserving
  + [open_fault] represents actual open API failure only
  + [query_fault] represents actual named query API failure only
  + [error_code] must be nonzero
  + [local_processing_failure] must not use either variant

& [RetainedContract] is unchanged except profile
  + [query_stages] remain file_id_info, final_volume_guid_path, volume_information, and remote_protocol_information
  + [root_identity] remains StrongFileIdentity
  + [final_path] remains canonical volume-GUID syntax
  + [volume] retains every 0.1 bound
  + [remote_protocol] retains every 0.1 bound
  + [disposition] retains the exact protocol and filesystem truth table
  + [protocol_zero] remains an invalidatable policy inference

& [LegacyContract] is fail closed
  + [result_profile_0_1] rejects during semantic validation
  + [request_result_profile_0_1] rejects
  + [unknown_field_variant_or_class] rejects during JSON decoding
  + [old_canonical_and_proof] remain immutable historical evidence

& [EffectContract] is zero
  + [windows_sys] is absent from the production module
  + [Windows_function_call] is absent
  + [unsafe] is absent
  + [filesystem_and_resource_ownership] are absent
  + [process_environment_clock_random_network_persistence] are absent
  + [fixture_candidate_scanner_receipt] effects are absent
  + [physical_claim] is absent
  + [Cargo_and_lock_delta] are zero

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-PFR-001 through M2B-PFR-012
  + [lineage] preserves source, research, prior authority, proof, and review
  + [profiles] fixes request 0.1 and result 0.2
  + [provenance] makes OS and local faults disjoint
  + [strictness] fixes fields, stages, classes, bounds, legacy, and unknown rejection
  + [closure] requires focused, global, static, evidence, rollback, support, and publication proof

& [Acceptance] is exact
  + [focused] request, four variants, three local classes, provenance, legacy, retained complete relation, bounds, and strict JSON pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [static] forbidden effect surface and Cargo delta are zero
  + [global] debug, overflow-checked release, format, lint, build, rustdoc, and audit pass
  + [evidence] every affected manifest is regenerated after durable narrative closure
  + [review] completed work recomputes readiness without runtime overclaim

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure revision only
  + [allowed] is safe-Rust request and result types, closed enum, validation, strict decoding, tests, evidence, and proof
  + [forbidden] is Windows API, pointer, buffer, raw or owned resource, FFI, unsafe, physical root, target-host observation, runtime wrapper, scanner, receipt, fixture, mutation, seal, cleanup, launch, promotion, or write authority

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + [source_preserved] is corrective raw source plus immutable manifest and prior bindings
  + [delineated] is request fault, OS open fault, OS query fault, local observation fault, and complete separated
  + [exploded] is twelve requirements, twelve constraints, ten failures, and ten verification gates
  + [semantically_refined] is exact request, OS error, local processing, complete, and nonclaim meaning
  + [constraint_checked] is official return semantics, Rust ownership preconditions, generated bindings, and prior proof
  + [pruned] is synthetic OS error, arbitrary prose, partial evidence, runtime, and scanner authority
  + [data_design_checked] is strict request product plus provenance-disjoint result sum
  + [exhaustion_reviewed] is seven_fold_phase_locked
  + [justified] is claim, support, false option, counterargument, invalidation, and rollback
  + [planned] is ordered authority, implementation, verification, evidence, and publication work
  + [registry_recorded] is graph-addressable nodes, causal edges, retrieval terms, and nonedges

